To customize the browsable API while maintaining the login/logout control, you must ensure your custom `rest_framework/api.html` template preserves the `userlinks` block.

When you override the `userlinks` block, you replace the default content, which includes the login/logout links. To add your own links while keeping the authentication controls, you must use `{{ block.super }}` within that block.

Example:
```html
{% extends "rest_framework/base.html" %}

{% block userlinks %}
    {{ block.super }}
    <li><a href="...">My Custom Link</a></li>
{% endblock %}
```

The `userlinks` block is defined as a list of links on the right of the header that contains the login/logout links by default.

